rule FavorableVariance
	lineageTag: a9cdedcf-b75c-5737-a890-227b9629d9a8
	statement: Variance is Actual minus Budget (or Forecast). For Revenue and other credit-nature accounts a positive variance is favorable; for Expense accounts a negative variance (underspend) is favorable. Favorable Variance = (Actual - Budget) x FavorableSign, so a positive value always means favorable. Use it when ranking performance across mixed account types. Source: Oracle EPM account type variance reporting.
	ruleReferencedEntity Account
		propertyScope: specific
		ruleReferencedProperty AccountType
		ruleReferencedProperty FavorableSign
	ruleReferencedEntity BudgetLine
		propertyScope: specific
		ruleReferencedProperty Amount
		ruleReferencedProperty ScenarioId
	ruleReferencedRelationship 'Line Posted To Account'
